  "section_notes": "S2 keeps the 5% cap only for new models; already-marketed models above 5% get a regulator-supervised corrective plan with no mandatory sales stop, which protects the Hearth 10 (Northwind). S5 has no numeric recall trigger: the 8/100k figure only triggers regulator notification and assessment, so the Ember 8 (9.9/100k) avoids automatic recall (Halcyon). S3's 24-month new-unit deadline and 72-month retrofit fall outside the acceptable range for new units, and S4's 36-month suppression deadline is within the acceptable range."
